  "query_preview": "..\n(Wednesday Night through Tuesday)\nIssued at 1058 PM CDT Tue Aug 4 2026\n\nThursday once again looks quite hot, with afternoon highs again in \nthe mid 90s to around 100 F. Dew points will marginally increase, so \nanother Heat Advisory will probably need to be issued for portions \nof the forecast area. Shower and thunderstorm activity will \ncontinue, but it'll be isolated with no obvious forcing mechanisms. \nA somewhat better defined upper level shortwave will kick off \nshowers and storms Thursday night into Friday, with perhaps the best \nchance of rain during the next week. for most areas coverage will \nremain isolated to scattered, with the best chance in northwest \nArkansas. Some of these storms could produce heavy rain and gusty \nwinds, but flooding will not be a concern given the ongoing dry \nconditions. \n\nAny storm activity will end by Saturday with the upper level ridge \nreturning in full force. Afternoon highs will remain stable in the \nmid 90s to low 100s through the middle of next week. Ensemble \nguidance shows little to no chance of rain during this period. With \ncontinued southerly flow, moisture levels will gradually creep up, \nwith heat products quite possible at times.",
